<body>
<header class="site-header"><div class="inner">
  <a class="brand" href="index.html">PowerCenter → dbt <span>explainer</span></a>
  <nav class="site-nav" id="site-nav" aria-label="Sections"></nav>
</div></header>

<main>
  <h1>Glossary</h1>
  <p class="lead">Our shared language. One word per idea, used the same way in code, tests, the README and our chats. This is what domain-driven design calls a ubiquitous language.</p>

  <div class="callout warn">
    <p><b>Words that clash.</b> PowerCenter and dbt use some of the same words for different things. Say which side you mean every time:</p>
    <p><b>Source:</b> say PC Source or dbt source. <b>Target:</b> say PC Target; in dbt, a target is an environment like dev. <b>Expression:</b> say Expression transformation (the box) or port expression (the formula). <b>Test:</b> say data test (dbt) or unit test (ours). <b>Link:</b> only between workflow tasks; between ports it's a connector.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="terms">Terms</h2>
  <input class="search" id="q" type="search" placeholder="Search terms, e.g. join, source, flag" aria-label="Search the glossary">
  <div class="chips" id="groups" role="group" aria-label="Filter by side"></div>
  <div class="g-list" id="list"></div>

  <h2 id="tables">Tables at a glance</h2>
  <p>The pipeline runs in layers: raw → staging → marts. Each table in the XML, which mapping writes it, and its twin in the reference project. Note that raw <i>stores</i> become <i>locations</i> from staging onwards.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
      <thead><tr><th>Table in the XML</th><th>Defined at</th><th>Written by</th><th>jaffle-shop twin</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="group"><td colspan="4">Raw: the input data. PC Sources only, nothing writes them.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RAW_CUSTOMERS</td><td><a class="L">L40</a></td><td>(seed data)</td><td>raw_customers</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RAW_ORDERS</td><td><a class="L">L26</a></td><td>(seed data)</td><td>raw_orders</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RAW_ITEMS</td><td><a class="L">L35</a></td><td>(seed data)</td><td>raw_items</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RAW_PRODUCTS</td><td><a class="L">L19</a></td><td>(seed data)</td><td>raw_products</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RAW_STORES</td><td><a class="L">L13</a></td><td>(seed data)</td><td>raw_stores</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RAW_SUPPLIES</td><td><a class="L">L6</a></td><td>(seed data)</td><td>raw_supplies</td></tr>
        <tr class="group"><td colspan="4">Staging: cleaned and renamed. Each is a PC Target here and a PC Source in the mart mappings.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>STG_CUSTOMERS</td><td><a class="L">L86</a></td><td>m_FL_JS_STAGING_FULL</td><td>stg_customers</td></tr>
        <tr><td>STG_ORDERS</td><td><a class="L">L67</a></td><td>m_FL_JS_STAGING_FULL</td><td>stg_orders</td></tr>
        <tr><td>STG_ORDER_ITEMS</td><td><a class="L">L62</a></td><td>m_FL_JS_STAGING_FULL</td><td>stg_order_items</td></tr>
