  <h1>Glossary</h1>
  <p class="lead">Our shared language. One word per idea, used the same way in code, tests, the README and our chats. This is what domain-driven design calls a ubiquitous language.</p>

  <div class="callout warn">
    <p><b>Words that clash.</b> PowerCenter and dbt use some of the same words for different things. Say which side you mean every time:</p>
    <p><b>Source:</b> say PC Source or dbt source. <b>Target:</b> say PC Target; in dbt, a target is an environment like dev. <b>Expression:</b> say Expression transformation (the box) or port expression (the formula). <b>Test:</b> say data test (dbt) or unit test (ours). <b>Link:</b> only between workflow tasks; between ports it's a connector.</p>
