1	<!doctype html>
2	<html lang="en">
3	<head>
4	<meta charset="utf-8">
5	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
6	<title>One Mapping, End to End</title>
7	<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/site.css">
8	<script src="assets/glossary-data.js"></script>
9	<script src="assets/example-data.js"></script>
10	<script src="assets/site.js"></script>
11	</head>
12	<body>
13	<header class="site-header"><div class="inner">
14	  <a class="brand" href="index.html">PowerCenter → dbt <span>explainer</span></a>
15	  <nav class="site-nav" id="site-nav" aria-label="Sections"></nav>
16	</div></header>
17	
18	<main>
19	  <h1>One mapping, end to end</h1>
20	  <p class="lead">We follow one small path through the XML: raw orders in, <code>STG_ORDERS</code> out. It is short, but it touches every piece: a PC Source, three kinds of box, a PC Target, and the session and workflow that run it.</p>
21	  <div class="callout">
22	    <p>The path lives inside mapping <code>m_FL_JS_STAGING_FULL</code> <a class="L">L90</a>, which writes 6 PC Targets. Here we look at the orders path only. All XML on this page was pulled from the file by a script. Attributes are trimmed to the ones that matter, and line numbers open GitHub.</p>
23	  </div>
24	
25	  <!-- ============ 1. who runs it ============ -->
26	  <h2>1 · Who runs it: workflow and session</h2>
27	  <p>The <a class="term" data-term="workflow">workflow</a> runs tasks in order. Each <a class="term" data-term="session">session</a> runs one mapping. Our path sits in the first session.</p>
28	  <figure>
29	    <div class="flow tight" role="img" aria-label="Workflow order: Start, then the staging session, then the core marts session, then the enriched marts session, then a command task.">
30	      <div class="flow-node dim"><span class="t">Start</span><span class="s"><a class="L">L4578</a></span></div>
31	      <div class="flow-arrow"><a class="L">L4623</a></div>
32	      <div class="flow-node hot"><span class="t">s_FL_JS_STAGING_FULL</span><span class="s">runs m_FL_JS_STAGING_FULL. <b>Our path is here.</b></span></div>
33	      <div class="flow-arrow"><a class="L">L4624</a></div>
34	      <div class="flow-node dim"><span class="t">s_FL_JS_MARTS_CORE</span><span class="s">core marts</span></div>
35	      <div class="flow-arrow"><a class="L">L4625</a></div>
36	      <div class="flow-node dim"><span class="t">s_FL_JS_MARTS_ENRICHED</span><span class="s">enriched marts</span></div>
37	      <div class="flow-arrow"><a class="L">L4622</a></div>
38	      <div class="flow-node dim"><span class="t">cmd_FL_JS_CREATE_RPT_VIEWS</span><span class="s"><a class="term" data-term="command-task">command task</a>, name only</span></div>
39	    </div>
40	    <figcaption>Workflow <code>wf_FL_JAFFLESHOP_DEMO</code> <a class="L">L4054</a> runs on demand <a class="L">L4056</a>. Each arrow is a <a class="term" data-term="workflow-link">workflow link</a>. The command task's command contains a credential, so we only show its name.</figcaption>
41	  </figure>
42	
43	  <h3>What the session adds</h3>
44	  <dl class="kv">
45	    <dt>Runs mapping</dt><dd><code>m_FL_JS_STAGING_FULL</code> <a class="L">L811</a></dd>
46	    <dt>Writes STG_ORDERS through</dt><dd>connection <code>STG_Jaffleshop</code> <a class="L">L4587</a>. The session itself says <code>MART_Jaffleshop</code> <a class="L">L912</a>, but the workflow's <a class="term" data-term="task-instance">task instance</a> overrides it, and the override wins. (Only names; the details live outside the file.)</dd>
47	    <dt>Load type</dt><dd>Bulk <a class="L">L913</a></dd>
48	    <dt>Truncate target first?</dt><dd>The session option says NO <a class="L">L919</a>, but the target's <a class="term" data-term="pre-sql">Pre SQL</a> empties it anyway: <code>TRUNCATE TABLE STG.STG_ORDERS</code> <a class="L">L541</a>. So every run is a full reload.</dd>
49	    <dt>Treat source rows as</dt><dd>Insert <a class="L">L995</a></dd>
50	  </dl>
51	  <p class="small muted">None of this changes <em>what</em> is computed. It is about <em>how</em> rows are written. dbt handles that with <a class="term" data-term="materialization">materialization</a>, which is still an open question.</p>
52	
53	  <div class="tabs-group">
54	    <div class="tabs" role="tablist">
55	      <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-wf" type="button">Workflow XML</button>
56	      <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-sess" type="button">Session XML</button>
57	    </div>
58	    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-wf" role="tabpanel"><pre id="code-wf"></pre></div>
59	    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-sess" role="tabpanel"><pre id="code-sess"></pre></div>
60	  </div>
61	
62	  <!-- ============ 2. the mapping path ============ -->
63	  <h2>2 · The mapping path: click a box</h2>
64	  <p>Five <a class="term" data-term="instance">instances</a> joined by <a class="term" data-term="connector">connectors</a>. The number on each arrow is how many connectors run between the two boxes.</p>
65	  <div class="flow tight" id="path"></div>
66	  <div class="panel" id="node-panel" aria-live="polite"></div>
67	
68	  <!-- ============ 3. the swap ============ -->
69	  <h2 id="swap">3 · Follow the connectors, not the names</h2>
70	  <p>The last hop, from the Sorter into the PC Target, is where names and connectors disagree. Toggle the view to see it.</p>
71	  <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Order of the right-hand column">
72	    <button type="button" id="mode-xml" aria-pressed="true">As in the XML</button>
73	    <button type="button" id="mode-name" aria-pressed="false">Lined up by name</button>
74	  </div>
75	  <figure>
76	    <svg class="diagram" id="swap-svg" role="img" aria-label="Ten connectors from SRT_ORDERS to STG_ORDERS. Six connect ports to columns with different names: dollar values go into the cents columns and cents go into the dollar columns."></svg>
77	    <figcaption id="swap-cap"></figcaption>
78	  </figure>
79	  <div class="callout warn">
80	    <p><b>What we do:</b> the SQL copies the connectors exactly, so <code>subtotal_cents</code> really holds dollars, and every one of these columns gets a <a class="term" data-term="flag">flag</a>. This is decision D1: we copy the XML, we don't fix it.</p>
81	  </div>
82	
83	  <!-- ============ 4. output ============ -->
84	  <h2 id="output">4 · The output: what the converter should write</h2>
85	  <p>Hand-written for now, to show the target. Each box becomes one <a class="term" data-term="cte">CTE</a>, the Sorter disappears, and the final <code>select</code> copies the connectors, flags included.</p>
86	  <div class="tabs-group">
87	    <div class="tabs" role="tablist">
88	      <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-sql" type="button">models/staging/stg_orders.sql</button>
89	      <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-yml" type="button">models/staging/sources.yml</button>
90	    </div>
91	    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-sql" role="tabpanel">
92	<pre class="code plain"><span class="cm">-- Generated from mapping m_FL_JS_STAGING_FULL, PC Target STG_ORDERS</span>
93	<span class="cm">-- Path: RAW_ORDERS → SQ_RAW_ORDERS → EXP_ORDERS → SRT_ORDERS → STG_ORDERS</span>
94	
95	with sq_raw_orders as (
96	    <span class="cm">-- Source Qualifier SQ_RAW_ORDERS (XML L161–180): no override, no filter</span>
97	    select id, customer, ordered_at, store_id, subtotal, tax_paid, order_total
98	    from {{ source('raw', 'raw_orders') }}
99	),
100	
101	exp_orders as (
102	    <span class="cm">-- Expression EXP_ORDERS (XML L106–125)</span>
103	    select
104	        id                            as order_id,
105	        customer                      as customer_id,
106	        store_id                      as location_id,
107	        date_trunc('day', ordered_at) as ordered_at_day,
108	        subtotal / 100                as subtotal,
109	        tax_paid / 100                as tax_paid,
110	        order_total / 100             as order_total,
111	        subtotal                      as subtotal_cents,
112	        tax_paid                      as tax_paid_cents,
113	        order_total                   as order_total_cents
114	    from sq_raw_orders
115	)
116	
117	<span class="cm">-- Sorter SRT_ORDERS (XML L513–533) dropped: row order has no meaning in a table.</span>
118	
119	select
120	    order_id,
121	    customer_id,
122	    location_id,
123	    ordered_at_day,
124	    subtotal          as subtotal_cents,     <span class="flagtxt">-- FLAG: dollars into a *_CENTS column (XML L608)</span>
125	    tax_paid          as tax_paid_cents,     <span class="flagtxt">-- FLAG: XML L609</span>
126	    order_total       as order_total_cents,  <span class="flagtxt">-- FLAG: XML L610</span>
127	    subtotal_cents    as subtotal,           <span class="flagtxt">-- FLAG: cents into a dollar column (XML L611)</span>
128	    tax_paid_cents    as tax_paid,           <span class="flagtxt">-- FLAG: XML L612</span>
129	    order_total_cents as order_total         <span class="flagtxt">-- FLAG: XML L613</span>
130	from exp_orders</pre>
131	    </div>
132	    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-yml" role="tabpanel">
133	<pre class="code plain">version: 2
134	
135	sources:
136	  - name: raw                 <span class="cm"># from PC Source OWNERNAME="RAW" (XML L26)</span>
137	    schema: raw
138	    tables:
139	      - name: raw_orders      <span class="cm"># from PC Source NAME="RAW_ORDERS" (XML L26)</span>
140	        columns:
141	          - name: id
142	          - name: customer
143	          - name: ordered_at
144	          - name: store_id
145	          - name: subtotal
146	          - name: tax_paid
147	          - name: order_total</pre>
148	    </div>
149	  </div>
150	  <p class="small muted">The folder name <code>staging/</code> is a placeholder; folder layout is still open.</p>
151	
152	  <h3>Does it run? One real row</h3>
153	  <p>We ran the SQL above in DuckDB on jaffle-shop's seed data, next to the reference model. Both return 61,948 rows. Here is the first order:</p>
154	  <div class="table-wrap">
155	    <table class="data">
156	      <thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>raw_orders.csv</th><th>Our stg_orders</th><th>Reference stg_orders</th></tr></thead>
157	      <tbody>
158	        <tr><td>order_id</td><td class="mono">9bed808a-…</td><td class="mono">9bed808a-…</td><td class="mono">9bed808a-…</td></tr>
159	        <tr><td>ordered_at_day</td><td class="mono">2024-09-01T15:01:00</td><td class="mono">2024-09-01 00:00</td><td class="mono">2024-09-01 00:00 <span class="muted">(named ordered_at)</span></td></tr>
160	        <tr class="flagged"><td>subtotal_cents</td><td class="mono">subtotal = 700</td><td class="mono">7.0</td><td class="mono">700</td></tr>
161	        <tr class="flagged"><td>tax_paid_cents</td><td class="mono">tax_paid = 42</td><td class="mono">0.42</td><td class="mono">42</td></tr>
162	        <tr class="flagged"><td>order_total_cents</td><td class="mono">order_total = 742</td><td class="mono">7.42</td><td class="mono">742</td></tr>
163	        <tr class="flagged"><td>subtotal</td><td></td><td class="mono">700</td><td class="mono">7.00</td></tr>
164	        <tr class="flagged"><td>tax_paid</td><td></td><td class="mono">42</td><td class="mono">0.42</td></tr>
165	        <tr class="flagged"><td>order_total</td><td></td><td class="mono">742</td><td class="mono">7.42</td></tr>
166	      </tbody>
167	    </table>
168	  </div>
169	  <div class="callout open">
170	    <p><b>Two lessons for check 3 (matching the reference):</b></p>
171	    <p>1. A faithful converter will <em>not</em> match the reference on these 6 columns. That's expected, so the comparison has to know about flags.<br>
172	    2. Column names differ too: <code>ordered_at_day</code> here (from the PC Target) and <code>ordered_at</code> in jaffle-shop. The comparison needs a column-name map.</p>
173	  </div>
174	
175	  <p style="margin-top:28px"><a href="steps.html">Next: how the converter gets from the XML to this SQL, in five steps →</a></p>
176	  <footer class="page-foot">Data: <code>assets/example-data.js</code>, generated from the XML. Row check run on 2026-11-21 against jaffle-shop seeds in DuckDB.</footer>
177	</main>
178	
179	<script>
180	(function () {
181	  var E = window.EXAMPLE;
182	  var byId = {};
183	  E.nodes.forEach(function (n) { byId[n.id] = n; });
184	
185	  /* ---------- section 1: code tabs ---------- */
186	  Site.renderCode(document.getElementById("code-wf"), E.workflow.lines);
187	  Site.renderCode(document.getElementById("code-sess"), E.session.lines);
188	
189	  /* ---------- section 2: clickable path ---------- */
190	  var INFO = {
191	    RAW_ORDERS: { kind: "PC Source", term: "pc-source",
192	      what: "Describes the raw orders table: 7 columns in schema RAW. It holds names and types only, no logic.",
193	      sql: "Declared once in sources.yml, then read as {{ source('raw', 'raw_orders') }}." },
194	    SQ_RAW_ORDERS: { kind: "Source Qualifier", term: "source-qualifier",
195	      what: "Reads the 7 columns into the mapping. Its SQL override, filter and join settings are all empty, so it reads everything as is.",
196	      sql: "The first CTE: select the 7 columns from the dbt source." },
197	    EXP_ORDERS: { kind: "Expression transformation", term: "expression-tx",
198	      what: "Renames 3 columns, keeps only the day of ORDERED_AT, divides the 3 money columns by 100, and also keeps the raw cent values. Its input ports end in _IN; connectors L647–649 feed them from SUBTOTAL, TAX_PAID and ORDER_TOTAL.",
199	      sql: "A CTE with one column per output port: renames, date_trunc, and / 100." },
200	    SRT_ORDERS: { kind: "Sorter", term: "sorter",
201	      what: "Sorts the rows by ORDER_ID, the only port with ISSORTKEY=YES. Distinct is NO, so no rows are removed.",
202	      sql: "Nothing. Row order has no meaning in a table, so the converter drops it and leaves a comment." },
203	    STG_ORDERS: { kind: "PC Target", term: "pc-target",
204	      what: "The table this path writes, with 10 columns. Look at the incoming connectors: in 6 of them the names don't match.",
205	      sql: "The final select. The model file is stg_orders.sql." }
206	  };
207	
208	  var path = document.getElementById("path");
209	  var panel = document.getElementById("node-panel");
210	  var buttons = [];
211	  E.nodes.forEach(function (n, i) {
212	    if (i > 0) {
213	      var w = E.wireCounts[i - 1];
214	      var arrow = document.createElement("div");
215	      arrow.className = "flow-arrow";
216	      arrow.textContent = w.count + " connectors";
217	      path.appendChild(arrow);
218	    }
219	    var b = document.createElement("button");
220	    b.type = "button";
221	    b.className = "flow-node " + (i === 0 ? "input" : i === E.nodes.length - 1 ? "output" : "");
222	    b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", "false");
223	    var t = document.createElement("span"); t.className = "t"; t.textContent = n.id;
224	    var s = document.createElement("span"); s.className = "s"; s.textContent = INFO[n.id].kind;
225	    b.appendChild(t); b.appendChild(s);
226	    b.addEventListener("click", function () { select(n.id); });
227	    path.appendChild(b);
228	    buttons.push([n.id, b]);
229	  });
230	  Site.breakAtUnderscores(path);
231	
232	  function h(tag, text, cls) { var e = document.createElement(tag); if (text != null) e.textContent = text; if (cls) e.className = cls; return e; }
233	
234	  function select(id) {
235	    buttons.forEach(function (p) { p[1].setAttribute("aria-pressed", p[0] === id ? "true" : "false"); });
236	    var n = byId[id], info = INFO[id];
237	    panel.innerHTML = "";
238	    var title = h("h3");
239	    title.appendChild(document.createTextNode(n.id + " "));
240	    var tag = h("a", info.kind, "tag");
241	    tag.href = "glossary.html#" + info.term;
242	    title.appendChild(tag);
243	    panel.appendChild(title);
244	    var p1 = h("p"); p1.appendChild(Site.textWithLines(info.what)); panel.appendChild(p1);
245	    var p2 = h("p"); p2.appendChild(h("b", "In SQL: ")); p2.appendChild(document.createTextNode(info.sql)); panel.appendChild(p2);
246	
247	    panel.appendChild(h("h4", "Definition in the XML", "muted small"));
248	    var pre = h("pre"); Site.renderCode(pre, n.lines); panel.appendChild(pre);
249	
250	    if (n.wiresIn.length) {
251	      panel.appendChild(h("h4", "Connectors coming in (" + n.wiresIn.filter(function (r) { return r[0] != null; }).length + ")", "muted small"));
252	      var flagged = E.flags.map(function (f) { return f.n; });
253	      var pre2 = h("pre"); Site.renderCode(pre2, n.wiresIn, { highlight: flagged }); panel.appendChild(pre2);
254	    } else {
255	      panel.appendChild(h("p", "No connectors come in: this is where data enters the mapping.", "small muted"));
256	    }
257	    var foot = h("p", null, "small muted");
258	    foot.appendChild(Site.textWithLines("Placed in the mapping as an instance at L" + n.instanceLine + "."));
259	    panel.appendChild(foot);
260	  }
261	  select("EXP_ORDERS");
262	
263	  /* ---------- section 3: swap diagram ---------- */
264	  var SVGNS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
265	  var srt = byId.SRT_ORDERS.lines.filter(function (r) { return /^<TRANSFORMFIELD/.test(r[1]); })
266	    .map(function (r) { return r[1].match(/NAME="([^"]+)"/)[1]; });
267	  var tgt = E.targetColumns.slice();
268	  var wires = byId.STG_ORDERS.wiresIn.filter(function (r) { return r[0] != null; }).map(function (r) {
269	    var a = {}; r[1].replace(/(\w+)="([^"]*)"/g, function (_, k, v) { a[k] = v; });
270	    return { n: r[0], from: a.FROMFIELD, to: a.TOFIELD, bad: a.FROMFIELD !== a.TOFIELD };
271	  });
272	
273	  function svgEl(tag, attrs, text) {
274	    var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);
275	    for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);
276	    if (text != null) e.textContent = text;
277	    return e;
278	  }
279	  function drawSwap(mode) {
280	    var svg = document.getElementById("swap-svg");
281	    var right = mode === "name" ? srt.slice() : tgt;   // by name: put each column opposite the port with the same name
282	    var ROW = 26, TOP = 44, LX = 172, RX = 292;
283	    var H = TOP + right.length * ROW;
284	    svg.setAttribute("viewBox", "0 0 470 " + H);
285	    while (svg.firstChild) svg.removeChild(svg.firstChild);
286	    svg.appendChild(svgEl("text", { x: LX, y: 18, "text-anchor": "end", "class": "hdr" }, "SRT_ORDERS ports"));
287	    svg.appendChild(svgEl("text", { x: RX, y: 18, "text-anchor": "start", "class": "hdr" }, "STG_ORDERS columns"));
288	    var badFrom = {}, badTo = {};
289	    wires.forEach(function (w) { if (w.bad) { badFrom[w.from] = 1; badTo[w.to] = 1; } });
290	    srt.forEach(function (p, i) {
291	      var y = TOP + i * ROW;
