19	  <h1>One mapping, end to end</h1>
20	  <p class="lead">We follow one small path through the XML: raw orders in, <code>STG_ORDERS</code> out. It is short, but it touches every piece: a PC Source, three kinds of box, a PC Target, and the session and workflow that run it.</p>
21	  <div class="callout">
22	    <p>The path lives inside mapping <code>m_FL_JS_STAGING_FULL</code> <a class="L">L90</a>, which writes 6 PC Targets. Here we look at the orders path only. All XML on this page was pulled from the file by a script. Attributes are trimmed to the ones that matter, and line numbers open GitHub.</p>
23	  </div>
24	
25	  <!-- ============ 1. who runs it ============ -->
26	  <h2>1 · Who runs it: workflow and session</h2>
27	  <p>The <a class="term" data-term="workflow">workflow</a> runs tasks in order. Each <a class="term" data-term="session">session</a> runs one mapping. Our path sits in the first session.</p>
28	  <figure>
