  <p>This is <code id="out-path"></code>, word for word, as <code>pc2dbt convert</code> wrote it. Each box is one <a class="term" data-term="cte">CTE</a>, the Sorter is dropped with a comment, and the final <code>select</code> follows the connectors, casts every column to its PC Target type and carries the <a class="term" data-term="flag">flags</a>.</p>
  <div class="tabs-group">
    <div class="tabs" role="tablist">
      <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-sql" type="button">models/m_fl_js_staging_full/stg_orders.sql</button>
      <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-yml" type="button">models/sources.yml</button>
    </div>
    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-sql" role="tabpanel"><pre class="code plain" id="out-sql"></pre></div>
    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab-yml" role="tabpanel"><pre class="code plain" id="out-yml"></pre></div>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted" id="flag-count"></p>

  <h3>Does it run? One real row</h3>
  <p id="row-lead"></p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
      <thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>raw_orders.csv</th><th>Our stg_orders</th><th>jaffle-shop stg_orders</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="row-body"></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">Highlighted rows carry a flag. Read across: our <code>subtotal_cents</code> holds the dollars (7, rounded by its type) and our <code>subtotal</code> holds the cents (700), the other way round from jaffle-shop.</p>
  <div class="callout decision">
    <p><b>Matching the reference.</b> A faithful copy can't match jaffle-shop on the crossed columns, and the names differ (<code>ordered_at_day</code> here, <code>ordered_at</code> there). So the check reads <code>tests/reference/expected_differences.yml</code>, which gives every known difference its reason, and fails on any difference without one (decision Q19).</p>
    <p id="staging-summary"></p>
    <p><a href="results.html">All three mappings, box by box, next to the SQL each box became: the Results page →</a></p>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ 5. history ============ -->
  <h2 id="history">5 · What this page said before the build</h2>
  <p>Section 4 was hand-written on 21 Nov 2026, before any converter code existed, to show the SQL we expected. Building the converter settled several things differently. Section 4 now shows the generated files, and a test (<code>tests/test_docs_fresh.py</code>) fails if the page and <code>out/</code> ever disagree.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
      <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Before the build (hand-written)</th><th>Now (generated)</th><th>Why it changed</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>ORDERED_AT_DAY <a class="L">L110</a></td><td class="mono">date_trunc('day', ordered_at)</td><td class="mono">strptime(strftime(…, '%d-%m-%y'), '%d-%m-%y')</td><td>Decision Q16: copy the XML's round trip through text, and flag that the two-digit year makes DuckDB guess the century. On this seed both give the same day, so the column still matches jaffle-shop.</td></tr>
        <tr class="flagged"><td>tax_paid_cents, first order</td><td class="mono">0.42</td><td class="mono">0</td><td>Decision Q11: the final select casts to the PC Target's type, <code>NUMBER(15,0)</code> <a class="L">L73</a>, so the dollars are rounded when written, as the original table would store them.</td></tr>
        <tr class="flagged"><td>subtotal_cents, first order</td><td class="mono">7.0</td><td class="mono">7</td><td>The same cast. <code>order_total_cents</code> is <code>NUMBER(12,2)</code>, so it keeps 7.42.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Column references</td><td class="mono">subtotal / 100</td><td class="mono">sq_raw_orders.subtotal / 100</td><td>Your answer in step 2: a bare name can mean the input or an output with the same name. DuckDB picks the input, but that is DuckDB's rule; a qualified name means one thing in any database.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Flags on stg_orders</td><td>6, all crossed connectors</td><td>12: 6 crossed, 5 rounding, 1 century</td><td>The rounding and century flags came with decisions Q11 and Q16.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Folder</td><td class="mono">models/staging/ (a placeholder)</td><td class="mono">models/m_fl_js_staging_full/</td><td>Decision Q8: one folder per mapping.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>sources.yml</td><td>column names only</td><td>names, data types and the PC Source's XML lines</td><td>The types come from the PC Source, so dbt and the reader see what the XML declares.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Conversion report</td><td>format still open</td><td><code>out/flags.md</code>: Flags, Not converted, Left out</td><td>Decisions Q10, Q17 and Q18.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Matching the reference</td><td>two lessons: the check must know about flags, and must map column names</td><td>an expected-differences list with a reason for each difference</td><td>Decision Q19. The staging result is in section 4; all three mappings are on the <a href="results.html">Results page</a>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">The hand-written version is in git history, in the first commit (630db46).</p>

